body:grpc {
  name: message 1
  content: '''
    {
      "requests": [
        { "object_id": "0x5" },
        { "object_id": "0x6" }
      ],
      "read_mask": {
        "paths": ["object_id", "version", "digest"]
      }
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  Fetch multiple objects by ID in a single call.

  **Service:** `sui.rpc.v2.LedgerService` · **Method:** `BatchGetObjects` (unary)

  **Request fields:**
  - `requests` (repeated GetObjectRequest): one entry per object to fetch.
  - `read_mask` (optional FieldMask): applied to every result; overrides any
    per-request read mask. Defaults to `object_id,version,digest`.

  **Response:** `objects` (repeated `GetObjectResult`) — each entry is
  either the requested `Object` or a `google.rpc.Status` error, so a
  not-found object doesn't fail the whole batch.

  Example uses `0x5` (SuiSystemState) and `0x6` (Clock), two singleton
  shared objects present on every network.

  Verified against `sui-mainnet.g.alchemy.com`.
}
